<title>FRANCE: Cr Foncier sit-in to run into next week.</title>
<headline>Cr Foncier sit-in to run into next week.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Staff occupying the headquarters of Credit Foncier for a 12th day on Tuesday decided to continue their sit-in until at least Wednesday of next week, a trade union spokesman at the troubled home loans group said.</p>
<p>There will be an extraordinary general assembly on February 5, which &quot;could take important decisions on the future of the group&quot;, the CGT union spokesman said.</p>
<p>The 3,300 staff at Credit Foncier, a home loans group, have mounted a powerful campaign against plans by Finance Minister Jean Arthuis for a break-up in which part of the business would be taken over by cooperatively run Credit Immobilier and the rest would be shut down over time.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
